{"availability":"available","full":"revaiew/revaiew-webmcp","name":"revaiew-webmcp","description":"A bounded WebMCP evidence-review demo for people and agents.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-04T06:41:56Z","updated":"2026-09-04T07:31:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://revaiew-webmcp.vercel.app","topics":["evidence","human-in-the-loop","nextjs","webmcp"],"demo":"https://revaiew-webmcp.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.824Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.824Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.824Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.824Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small, inspectable WebMCP challenge demo. A compatible browser agent can read a fixed public mathematics corpus through five page-scoped tools and stage one visible evidence packet through a sixth tool. The tool boundary ends there: a registered tool cannot choose, confirm, or create a receipt. The visible browser interface presents the decision and confirmation, and only that application path creates the SHA-256-bound receipt. Browser and agent behavior remains subject to normal user-control policies; this demo does not prove a browser-generic ban on automation."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/revaiew/revaiew-webmcp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d80c816a4a3353624bf3008a6a12c88c7d2b07dc3a8b9c44ff1305dfc6909844","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.933Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:07.933Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A small, inspectable WebMCP challenge demo. A compatible browser agent can read a fixed public mathematics corpus through five page-scoped tools and stage one visible evidence packet through a sixth tool. The tool boundary ends there: a registered tool cannot choose, confirm, or create a receipt. The visible browser interface